CI evidence and decisions

Run 32491165457 exposed three independent contract gaps. Complete Windows backend tests ran 3616 passing tests but two inherited-pipe fixtures failed: pass_fds is Unix-only, and the 50 ms deadline expired before loaded Windows Python wrote its descendant PID. The fixtures now use inheritable descriptors with close_fds=False on every OS. Unix keeps the 50 ms deadline; Windows gets 2 seconds solely so Python starts before the same global-deadline behavior is exercised.

Windows strict Clippy also found PythonRuntime test helpers unused after Unix fake-executable tests were correctly gated. No dead-code allowance was added. A Windows-only test now reads the actual test interpreter version and exercises resolve_with_path against its real executable directory.

The Linux persistence contract correctly detected that SearXNG data_dir ownership moved from process.rs into paths.rs and process_receipt.rs. The single expected-reference authority now records the exact current distribution: paths 2, process 2, process_receipt 1.

Executed locally with Rust 1.98.0: cargo fmt --check; cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings; inherited-pipe deadline test 5 consecutive passes; successful-parent cleanup test 3 consecutive passes; SearXNG 85 passed and 1 release-wheelhouse test ignored; persistence migration 9 passed; CI script contracts 16 passed; graphify update completed.

The new Windows resolver test and portable inherited-handle behavior still require the native PR runner. This note does not claim Windows success before that run is green.

Follow-up evidence: native run 32493403293 invalidated the Windows resolver test and showed that descendant cleanup still skipped exited roots. Commit cded095e removes that false resolver proof and fixes Windows liveness at the central process_exists authority. Treat the native claims in this note as attempted coverage, not successful coverage.
